{
  "id": "Compound::DB00635 - Gene::2908",
  "verbalization": "Prednisone is linked to Nr3c1 through a series of molecular interactions that involve glucocorticoid receptors. The evidence suggests that Prednisone, as a corticosteroid hormone receptor agonist, binds to Nr3c1, which is a key component of the glucocorticoid receptor complex. This binding is supported by multiple paths, including direct interactions with Alclometasone and Methylprednisolone, both of which are glucocorticoids. The shared ancestry of these compounds in the Therapeutic Glucocorticoid and Primary Alpha-Hydroxy Ketone categories further reinforces the role of Nr3c1 in the signaling pathways of glucocorticoids. The consistent presence of Nr3c1 as a binding partner across different glucocorticoid analogs indicates a fundamental role in the cellular response to these compounds. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Nr3c1 in mediating the effects of glucocorticoids, with Prednisone serving as a representative of this class that directly influences Nr3c1's function.",
